solutions:
To find the total number of squares in the figure, we can count each possible square type and then add them up.

1. Count the $1 \times 1$ squares:
   \begin{align*}
   \text{There are 21 of these squares.}
   \end{align*}

2. Count the $2 \times 2$ squares:
   \begin{align*}
   \text{There are 12 of these squares.}
   \end{align*}

3. Count the $3 \times 3$ squares:
